{
  "evidence": "- TEXT_C: Cancel Trident; refocus defence to security and peace; end arms export promotion. Replace the Home Office with a Ministry for Sanctuary; humane immigration; halve the prison population; replace prohibition with a regulated drugs system; legal cannabis. Universal Basic Income; 10:1 pay ratio cap; Living Wage £12; strong equality agenda (LGBTIQA+ rights, self‑ID). Ecocide law; GM moratorium; phase‑in tax on meat/dairy; ban hunting/trail hunting; phase out animal testing.\n- TEXT_D: “Protect the Union”; NATO 2% defence; maintain a minimal nuclear deterrent; £1bn for community policing; Online Crime Agency. 1p on Income Tax ringfenced for NHS and social care; new mental‑health waiting‑time standards; 24/7 crisis care. Fair‑tax package (Corporation Tax 20%, Commercial Landowner Levy), UK2050 plan, Skills Wallet; workers’ rights reform without pay‑ratio caps or UBI. Climate action and nature protection targets without bans on GM or meat/dairy taxes.",
  "reasoning": "The electorate profile places highest weight on loyalty and care, with moderate emphasis on authority and proportionality and low priority on sanctity. TEXT_D better matches this mix by foregrounding national unity and defence commitments (loyalty/authority) while still offering strong care/equality provisions, and it avoids the stronger purity framing and anti‑authority/egalitarian‑maximizing moves (UBI, pay caps, dismantling the Home Office) that characterise TEXT_C.",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "winner": "TEXT_D"
}
